<title>USA: Monroe County, N.Y., announces $140 mln sale.</title>
<headline>Monroe County, N.Y., announces $140 mln sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The County of Monroe, New York, announced the sale of approximately $140 million general obligation refunding bonds during the week of November 18th through negotiated sale by a group led by First Albany Corporation.</p>
<p>These bonds will be issued to refund all or part of the following issues:</p>
<p>$1,130,000 Public Improvement (Serial) Bonds 1986</p>
<p>$9,040,000 Water Improvement Refunding (Serial) Bonds, 1987</p>
<p>$2,190,000 Public Improvement Refunding (Serial) Bonds, 1987</p>
<p>$2,950,000 Water Improvement (Serial) bonds 1987</p>
<p>$63,370,000 Public Improvement Serial Bonds - 1992</p>
<p>$8,450,000 Water Improvement Serial Bonds - 1992</p>
<p>$78,420,499 Public Improvement Bonds - 1994 The issuance of the refunding bonds is subject to market conditions as well as the county's right to postpone or cancel this sale.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
